//
// GEMMA4-E4B Q4NX prefill TTFT vs prompt length, into
// gemma4_e4b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark).
// The counterpart to run_npu2_sweep.lit (decode tok/s vs KV depth). They cannot
// share a table: one is latency against problem size, the other throughput
// against cache depth.
//
// It times the fused prefill (fused_prefill/), which is chunked and takes any
// prompt up to the length it was built for, so sweep_prefill.py --fused builds
// it once, for the longest length, and times every length in one process on a
// synthetic prompt of exactly that length.
// run_npu2_verify_fused_prefill_8k.lit gates the same build at 8k tokens.
//
// Latency only, never a correctness gate.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, peano_ge22, hfweights_fastflowlm_gemma4_e4b_it_npu2
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_prefill.py --model-name gemma4_e4b_q4nx --makefile %S/Makefile --lengths 512,1024,2048,4096,8192,32768 --fused --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out gemma4_e4b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < gemma4_e4b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "gemma4_e4b_q4nx"
// CHECK: "axis": "prefill_len"
// A parsed number at the reference length, not just a well-formed file: if the
// bench's timing line drifts out of sweep_prefill.py's regex every point goes
// null and the published curve silently empties while the test stays green.
// CHECK: "prefill_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
